==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*streyg-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|cōnstrictus||compressed, contracted}}, past participle of {{m|la|cōnstringō||to draw or bind together; to compress}}. {{doublet|en|constrain}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kənˈstɹɪkt/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-constrict.wav |Audio (RP)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪkt|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[narrow]], especially by application of [[pressure]].
# {{q|of a [[snake]]}} To [[coil]] around ([[prey]]) in order to [[asphyxiate]] it.
# {{lb|en|figurative}} To [[limit]] or [[restrict]].
#: {{syn|en|inhibit}}

